12. Function Hoisting
        greet();

        function greet() {
          console.log("Hello");
        }
    Answer:
        ✅ Output: "Hello"
        👉 Function declarations are hoisted.

13. Function Expression Hoisting
        sayHi();

        var sayHi = function () {
          console.log("Hi");
        };
    Answer:
        ✅ Output:
        ❌ Error: sayHi is not a function
        Because variable hoisted as undefined.

14. let vs var hoisting
        console.log(a);
        var a = 10;

        console.log(b);
        let b = 20;
    Answer:
        undefined
        ReferenceError

15. Closure Output
        function outer() {
          let x = 10;
          return function inner() {
            console.log(x);
          };
        }

        const fn = outer();
        fn();
    Answer:
        ✅ Output: 10
        👉 Inner remembers outer variable.

